AIS (Automatic Identification System) Maritime Tracker
-------------------------------------------------------
Name: William Eykyn
Date: 1/31/26
Project: AIS Maritime Tracking
Description: Containerized Python application for live AIS vessel tracking and 
             map visualization.

------ Setup ------

1. Obtain a free AISStream API Key
    - Go to: https://aisstream.io/documentation
    - Scroll to the section titled “Authentication”
    - Click on "Get Started" button on top of screen & sign in using GitHub
    - Generate a new AIS API key for free 

2. Create your environment file
    - Copy the example environment file:
        cp .env.example .env
    - Open .env and replace: "YOUR_API_KEY_HERE" with your newly generated 
      AISStream API Key.

3. Run directly from Docker Hub 
    In your terminal, run commands: 
        - docker pull willeykyn/aismaritimetracker:latest
        - docker run --rm --env-file .env -v $(pwd):/app willeykyn/aismaritimetracker

    This will:
    - Downloads the pre-built Docker image from Docker Hub
    - Run the containerized AIS tracking script
    - Generate an interactive map as an HTML file called "map.html"

4. View the map
    - Open map.html in your browser to view the live AIS vessel map.
    - Refresh map periodically to see updated locations and pings from 
      new vessels.
    - If you are having issues with the map (such as "403r Access blocked"), 
      serve the map locally using the following commands:
        
        Run: 
        python3 -m http.server 8000
        Then open:
        http://localhost:8000/map.html

